## SPRINT 14 — Production Runtime, Real Agent Execution & AG-001 ↔ AG-002 Runtime Wiring

### IMPORTANT

This is a production-focused implementation sprint.

Do NOT redesign AG-001 or AG-002.
Do NOT rewrite working code unnecessarily.
Do NOT start AG-003 or AG-004 yet.
Do NOT add fake/mock production implementations.
Do NOT silently bypass security, authorization, persistence, lifecycle, or error handling.

Use the existing architecture and contracts wherever possible.

The current baseline is:

* AG-001 Master Orchestrator implemented and heavily tested
* AG-002 Memory Manager implemented and heavily tested
* PostgreSQL/Neon durable persistence implemented
* Retrieval and Context Integration implemented
* Security/authorization implemented
* Event log/replay/DSR implemented
* 1246 tests passing
* Typecheck clean
* Lint clean
* Build successful

The remaining major blockers are:

1. No proper production composition root
2. AG-001 ↔ AG-002 is not fully wired as a real runtime dependency graph
3. ExecutionEngine has no real production AgentExecutor path
4. Runtime events are not fully emitted from actual operations
5. There is no complete end-to-end runtime path from request → orchestrator → agent → memory → response

Your job is to remove these blockers.

