# PHASE 1 — Production Composition Root

Create a clean production composition root.

The application must have one authoritative place responsible for constructing production dependencies.

It should construct and connect:

```text
Configuration
   ↓
Storage
   ↓
Repository
   ↓
Memory Services
   ↓
Memory Manager
   ↓
Memory Context Provider
   ↓
Event Log
   ↓
Agent Registry
   ↓
Agent Executor
   ↓
Execution Engine
   ↓
Routing / Planning
   ↓
Master Orchestrator
   ↓
Application Runtime
```

Requirements:

* No production dependency should rely on test doubles.
* No circular dependency.
* No duplicate singleton instances of critical services.
* Dependencies should be explicitly injectable.
* Production composition must honor environment configuration.
* Durable mode must use PostgreSQL/Neon.
* Never silently fall back from durable PostgreSQL to in-memory storage.
* Fail closed on invalid production configuration.
* Startup must validate critical dependencies.
* Shutdown must gracefully close resources such as PostgreSQL pools.
* Configuration errors must be typed and actionable.
* Secrets must never be printed in startup logs.

Add tests for:

* successful composition
* invalid configuration
* durable storage initialization
* missing database URL
* dependency identity
* graceful shutdown
* no test-double usage in production composition

