# PHASE 4 — First Real Runtime Agent

Create a minimal but REAL built-in runtime agent so that the complete pipeline can actually execute.

This is NOT the final intelligent agent system.

It is the first production-compatible execution target used to validate the runtime architecture.

The agent should:

* receive structured execution context
* receive memory context when requested
* produce a deterministic structured response
* expose capabilities
* integrate through AgentRegistry
* execute through the production AgentExecutor
* generate runtime events

Do not hard-code the orchestrator to this agent.

The agent must be registered through the normal registry mechanism.

Design it so future AG-003/AG-004/LLM-backed agents can plug into the same interface.

